# Engineering governance

RulePackVersion: 1.7.0

## MUST

- Domain logic must not depend on UI or infrastructure details.
- Prefer constructor injection over service locators and static mutable globals in domain code.
- One writer per mutable concern; orchestrators use abstractions for time, IO, persistence.
- Rule of Three for abstractions (except DI/test interfaces).
- SOLID: flag god types, fat constructors (about five+ deps), DIP inversions, kitchen-sink interfaces.
- No secrets in code; validate external input at boundaries.
- One primary type per file; no large blocks of commented-out dead code.
- Flag enum-only files when the enum is owned by one type (should be nested); separate file only if shared or a public cross-boundary contract.
- Flag unresolved WIP markers (TODO/FIXME/HACK/TEMP/WIP, stubs, #if false) as debt.
- Comments explain why - not setup tutorials; flag inconsistent comment/`///` density vs sibling types.
- Tests in the same batch: flag framework theater and obvious missing high-value cases when test files are supplied.

## Audit focus

1. Service locator / static mutable state in domain logic
2. Layer violations (Core referencing UI, etc.)
3. Naming and comment/`///` density consistency
4. Class size and responsibility (SOLID / fat constructors)
5. Enum-only files owned by a single type (prefer nest in owner)
6. Null/wiring handling at boundaries
7. Comment quality (rationale vs imperative setup)
8. Missing or redundant XML documentation on public API
9. WIP / stub / dead commented-out debt
10. Test excess or obvious high-value gaps when tests are in scope
11. Hot-path performance smells (evidence-minded; no invented metrics)
